ally queen to e8 to check  because that would be  a a double attack here and if you go  queen to d8 that  will help out with the defense uh then  just rook captures on f7 king captures  rook to f1 check the bishop covers the  h7 square so that's going to be an issue  and after the king moves just queen e4  you're going to get checkmated the real  covers df file there is no defending  this  so uh very nice so after knight g5 we  have f5 instead of the h6 now preventing  this bishop  from being of any use but not really  adiban finds another great idea and that  is  c5 c5 is the only good move for white  here and that makes it all the  uh all the better for for white to find  this it it kind of  blocks the queen from entering the game  right away but also  has the immediate thread of queen to a  to check and then you're just getting  crushed with knight to f7 check and so  on  so here king the h8 preventing this and  now  queen to e2 so again what do you play  here  uh well uh you could play queen captures  on c5 this is uh  black's most resilient reply uh but  still queen h5 goes after the h7 pawn h6  and again knight  to f7 check king g8 knight captures on  h6g captures and now that we have this  very standard checkmating pattern king  h8 queen captures king goes back queen  g6 check king h8  and now of course a very nice rook lift  and that's it black is now getting  checkmated  and of course you can play this to guard  the h3 square with your bishop because  then  well you're getting checkmated again so  instead after queen to a2 we have knight  to d7 but now  we've actually reached our first pause  the video moment so feel free to pause  the video here  and try to find the only one move that  wins the game for adiban while i give  you a couple of seconds  so uh for those of you who were able to  do it congratulations on  not stopping for anything uh and for  those of you who just want to enjoy the  show it's  knight captures on h7 as i'm sure many  of you guys  f